{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PATCHSET 2 pushed to Gerrit 1344, clearing BOTH -1 votes from patchset 1.\n\n--- BLOCK 1: LLM-Review-1 (bugfix-size-attestation) — CLEARED, no LLM spend ---\nNot a code finding: 554 non-test lines exceeds the 150-line floor for a bug fix, so the Gerrit\nbugfix-size gate demanded a certified plan-review attestation, and the record read\n\"unsigned; no plan-review attestation record\". A recorded REVIEW_RESULT sidecar already existed\nand was merely stale, so `rebar sign-review 129e-2d88-cce2-492c` re-signed it from that sidecar\nwith NO review re-run:\n  {\"ok\": true, \"signed\": true, \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n   \"reason\": \"re-signed the plan-review attestation from the latest REVIEW_RESULT sidecar\n              (no LLM review re-run)\"}\nSigned at d39bc122d756bcd76ef638dfd606b24812bbb349 (= origin/main at push time). Verified the\nSIGNATURE event reached the remote: commit 4a0c1358be on origin/tickets, and the local store HEAD\nis an ancestor of origin/tickets, so the review bot can see it.\n\n--- BLOCK 2: Verified-1 — DIAGNOSED AND FIXED. It was NOT the stale-base trap. ---\nRun 30873144317 failed the SAME way on all four matrix legs (ubuntu 3.11/3.12/3.13 + macos 3.13):\n  FAILED tests/unit/test_web_tool_gating.py::test_runner_attaches_web_capability_on_every_provider[bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8]\n  FAILED tests/unit/test_web_tool_gating.py::test_runner_unflagged_request_is_byte_identical[bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8]\n  2 failed, 9814 passed  — a genuine 2-test failure, not a missing gate script.\n\nROOT CAUSE — a host-dependent test of MY OWN, not a production defect. Both cases are the\nbedrock leg of a provider-parametrized test. Only the Agent class is doubled (via the\n`_import_pydantic_ai` seam); the MODEL/PROVIDER is still built for real, and\n`build_bedrock_provider` resolves BOTH a region and credentials at construction time. This host\nhas both in its ambient AWS config, so the tests passed locally; CI has neither, so they failed.\nThe suite cited earlier (9863 passed) was therefore green only because of ambient host config.\n\nReproduced locally before fixing, by stripping exactly what CI lacks:\n  env -u AWS_DEFAULT_REGION -u AWS_REGION -u AWS_PROFILE HOME=<empty dir> pytest tests/unit/test_web_tool_gating.py\n  -> 2 failed, 18 passed — the identical two cases, the identical LLMConfigError.\n\nBoth failure arms were then measured separately:\n  * no region -> LLMConfigError from build_bedrock_provider's boto3 region pre-check;\n  * region pinned but no credentials -> botocore reaches for IMDS and trips the repo's\n    network-forbidden fixture (\"Network access is forbidden in unit/scripts tests\").\nSo pinning the region ALONE is insufficient — the first fix attempt proved exactly that by\nstill failing.\n\nFIX (test-only, 13 lines in tests/unit/test_web_tool_gating.py::_agent_kwargs):\n  * region via the LLMConfig FIELD (`bedrock_region_name=\"us-east-1\"`), deliberately NOT via\n    REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION — that env var is read only by LLMConfig's env/table factory\n    (config.py:578), never by the direct construction this helper does, so a monkeypatched env\n    var silently falls through to boto3's ambient resolution and keeps the host-dependence.\n    (Measured: the env-var attempt did not change the result.)\n  * credentials via botocore's env provider (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\n    placeholders), which short-circuits the IMDS lookup.\nMirrors the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY placeholder the same helper already sets. No client call is made,\nso neither value is used. NO production file changed.\n\nVERIFIED both directions:\n  faithful CI sim (no AWS env, empty HOME): 20 passed\n  this host (ambient AWS config present):   20 passed\nThe case is now hermetic instead of passing for the wrong reason.\n\nPer the standing decision, `max_uses`/`blocked_domains`/`allowed_domains` were left on the native\ntool instance — hoisting them to the capability level flips pydantic-ai's `_requires_native()` True\nand suppresses the local fallback. The guard pinning `get_toolset() is not None` still passes.\n\n--- FULL GATE RUN at 6700cf8ddd, clean tree, judged by exit code only ---\ngit status --porcelain: EMPTY before the suite run cited below.\nPASS: uv lock --check · make lint · make typecheck · make config-check ·\n      check_verify_gate_parity · check_comment_hygiene · check_raw_git_writes ·\n      check_wall_clock_asserts · check_config_reads · check_docs_index --check ·\n      check_readme_quickstart · check_server_manifest · gen_env_registry.py --check ·\n      security_pin\nGenerators (gen_cli_reference / gen_mcp_reference / gen_env_registry) re-run: left the tree clean.\nFULL DEFAULT SUITE: 9879 passed, 34 skipped, 0 failed in 471.94s\n  (pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 6 --dist worksteal)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785821891884424001,"uuid":"4e1ac50b-f427-4bae-92b7-bc2779f3cfbf"}